        "id": 100,
        "question": "Why do businesses choose Luxembourg?",
        "answer": "Luxembourg offers political stability, access to the European Union, an advanced financial sector, and a favourable environment for international business.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": 101,
        "question": "What company types are commonly established in Luxembourg?\n",
        "answer": "Businesses commonly establish SARL, SA, SOPARFI holding companies, investment funds, and specialised financial structures depending on their objectives.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": 102,
        "question": "Is Luxembourg part of the European Union?\n",
        "answer": "Yes. Companies established in Luxembourg benefit from access to the EU single market and the European regulatory framework.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": 103,
        "question": "Who regulates the financial sector in Luxembourg?\n",
        "answer": "The Commission de Surveillance du Secteur Financier (CSSF) regulates financial institutions, investment firms, and other financial market participants.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": 104,
        "question": "How long does it take to set up a company?\n",
